@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option desk - How data flows (every arrow is an artifact on disk)

database "Provider\n(Yahoo / Alpha Vantage)" as provider
component "chain\nchain_SYM_EXPIRY.json\nquotes + per-contract implied vol\n+ counts.without_iv" as chain #C6E9C6
component "greeks\ngreeks_SYM_EXPIRY.json\n16 Greeks per contract,\nunits block, skip counts" as greeks
component "exposure\nexposure_SYM_EXPIRY.json\ngamma by strike, walls, flip,\nmax pain, ratios, smile" as exposure
component "strategy\nstrategy_SYM_NAME_EXPIRY.json\nlegs, risk graph, probabilities,\nnet Greeks, friction, payoff" as strategy
component "compare\ncomparison_SYM_EXPIRY.json\nevery structure scored and ranked,\nwith the ranking caveat" as compare
component "simulate\nsimulation_SYM_Nd.json\nposterior, diagnostics, fan,\nVaR and ES, per-structure dists" as sim
component "backtest\nbacktest_SYM_STRAT_Nd.json\ntrades, statistics, significance,\nbenchmark, honesty statement" as bt
component "forward\nforward_ledger.json\npositions, marks,\nsettlements, thesis" as forward
component "Dashboard\nreads artifacts, writes nothing\n?u=SYM&e=EXPIRY addressable" as dash

provider --> chain : quotes
provider --> sim : daily closes
provider --> bt : daily closes
chain --> greeks
chain --> exposure
chain --> strategy
strategy --> compare
strategy --> sim : per-structure\ndistributions
strategy --> forward
chain --> forward : marks
greeks --> dash
exposure --> dash
compare --> dash
sim --> dash
bt --> dash
forward --> dash

note bottom of chain
Replaced artifacts move to
archive/<date>/ with a timestamp:
the 595-solved / 12-refused chain
became 590 / 17 six hours later,
and both remain provable.
end note

note right of sim
simulate and backtest read the
underlying's price history, not the
chain: they answer questions about
the underlying's own behaviour,
so the dashboard files them under
the symbol, not an expiry.
end note

note bottom of dash
Every artifact carries the same meta block:
schema, timestamp, tool, versions,
provider used, degraded + reason, notes,
disclaimer and licence note.
end note

caption Eight schemas under shell/src/optiondesk/contracts/. The schema is the interface: skills, MCP, dashboard and third parties read artifacts, never Python objects.
@enduml
